    {
      "id": "the-first-part-of-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_12.2/p@52105",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "BURGUNDY.\nMyself, as far as I could well discern\nFor smoke and dusky vapors of the night,\nAm sure I scared the Dauphin and his trull,\nWhen arm in arm they both came swiftly running,\nLike to a pair of loving turtle-doves\nThat could not live asunder day or night.\nAfter that things are set in order here,\nWe’ll follow them with all the power we have.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
